"""E4 extension (PREREG_AMENDMENTS A11): instrumented ProtoGLAD (arXiv 2602.10708) runs on UB-GOLD folds.

Same CLI and per-run JSON "part" schema as evalpaper/harness/run_eval.py:
  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -B run_method.py --method ProtoGLAD --dataset BZR --fold 0 [--hp hpfree]
Grid replay of ProtoGLAD's own test-AUC hyperparameter search (NOTES.md):
  python -B run_method.py grid --dataset BZR --fold 0 --psi1 64      # one unit = (dataset, fold, psi1), 24 cells
  python -B run_method.py select --dataset BZR                        # needs all 30 units of the dataset

* ProtoGLAD's code is the official repository at commit f7d8ce9 (src/, byte-identical, no license: run only).
  The pipeline below is a line-by-line copy of src/protoglad/experiments/run_detection.py: run_single_trial()
  split into stage 1 (node IK + WL) and stage 2 (graph IK + prototypes + scoring); every change is marked
  "# CHANGE" and listed in NOTES.md (D1-D5).
* Folds, features, seeds and the held-out normals come from the harness itself (its run_eval.py is imported,
  never modified): UB-GOLD get_ad_split_TU / get_ad_dataset_TU, asserted against
  $GLAD_DATA_ROOT/ubgold_splits, set_seed(3407+fold), RandomState(2026+1000*fold) carve-out.
* hp 'ubgold' (= 'tuned', NOTES.md): UB9 -> the test-grid-best cell of the replay (test-label-selected upper bound);
  MUTAG -> the README eval-mode line. hp 'hpfree' -> config.py defaults.
* One evaluation point per run (no epochs): meta.hparams num_epoch = eval_freq = 1, so ORACLE = LAST = VAL-NORMAL.

Outputs (EP_PARTS / EP_SCORES / EP_GRID override):
  evalpaper/ext/parts/<run_id>.json                           meta + the single evaluation record
  $GLAD_DATA_ROOT/ext_protoglad/scores/<run_id>.npz         per-graph test / held-out scores
  $GLAD_DATA_ROOT/ext_protoglad/grid/<feat>/<DS>/fold<f>_psi1_<p>.{json,npz}   grid units
  evalpaper/ext/ProtoGLAD/results/grid/<DS>[_native]_{grid.csv,gridbest.json}   replay summaries
